0..68 Comment "//! A rule of a commutative operation fires in the two orders of its"
69..83 Comment "//! arguments."
84..87 Comment "//!"
88..164 Comment "//! The theory of a tally states that its meet is commutative. A reader then"
165..242 Comment "//! expects the empty tally to absorb on each side of a meet. The rule states"
243..290 Comment "//! the absorption for the first argument only."
291..294 Comment "//!"
295..372 Comment "//! The match of a rule tries the two orders of the arguments of the meet. So"
373..447 Comment "//! the rule `meet none x <=> none` decides `meet x none` also. The kernel"
448..493 Comment "//! replays each rewriting by the same match."
494..497 Comment "//!"
498..514 Comment "//! - see: #8299"
516..573 Comment "// `Tally`, its two rules that rewrite, and its symmetry."
